-        f"sh.Run {q(command_line)}, 0, False",
+        # Window style 0 = hidden. bWaitOnReturn True keeps wscript alive for the life of python.exe.
+        # False used to detach and let wscript exit 0, so the task went Ready and RestartOnFailure
+        # never observed the gateway's exit 75 (#86098 / #87001). The loop is the supervisor: it
+        # restarts only after the child has actually exited. 0 is a planned stop. 78 is the permanent
+        # config refusal (GATEWAY_FATAL_CONFIG_EXIT_CODE); quitting 0 parks the task instead of
+        # respawning a refusal forever. Exit 75 always uses the short delay. Five consecutive
